      "mergeID": "693aec8545a83eebbdbe8122",
      "mergedPostDetails": "When tasking selfies using the Flip Camera button ever since the latest update, images are now saved as flipped. I know that the newest update fixed the Flip Camera button to show the viewfinder in reverse just like it does on a real camera (https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/vrchat-202523), however it now SAVES flipped as well, requiring the player to manually flip the image in their own editor to get the image back to the correct orientation. This is not the correct behavior nor is it how images saved before, as they would save in the correct perspective prior to this update, just like a real selfie camera would. Just like on your phone, the viewfinder would show it flipped the wrong way, but then save the correct way. It seems as if now images are not flipping themselves to the correct orientation before saving, almost as if it is taking a direct screen grab from the Viewfinder itself. \n\nDesired result: Images taken in the Flip Camera/Selfie mode should save in the opposite orientation of the Viewfinder. Without this, the user has to manually edit their photos, or avoid using the flip camera function.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[CAMERA] Selfie Images are now Inverted/Flipped when saving",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "685ee6c093e47313f7893506",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
