      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Adding to this, because it has caused a bit of confusion, especially with taking selfies or group photos while utilizing the flip button on the default mode camera. I understand that while in flying mode, you can click to mirror the image horizontally. But it also affects the camera while in default mode as well (holding the camera in hand and clicking the button to put it into selfie mode). In default mode, instead of rotating the camera 180 degrees, it inverts the camera's view, causing the image to save reversed as if I had clicked the flying camera's mirroring button instead. My only solution around this has been to physically rotate the camera around after pulling it out.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
